By difference of squares on the equation $a^2 - b^2 = 36,$ $(a + b)(a - b) = 36,$ so
\[a + b = \frac{36}{a - b} = 9.\]With the equation $a - b = 4,$ we can solve to get $a = \frac{13}{2}$ and $b = \frac{5}{2}.$

