solution:
To start, we can clearly draw $1\times1$,$2\times2$,$3\times3$,and $4\times4$ squares.  Next, we must consider the diagonals.  We can draw squares with sides of $\sqrt{2}$ and $2\sqrt{2}$ as shown: [asy]
