Let $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ $d,$ and $e$ be the distinct roots of the equation $x^5 + 7x^4 - 2 = 0.$  Find
\begin{align*}
&\frac{a^5}{(a - b)(a - c)(a - d)(a - e)} + \frac{b^5}{(b - a)(b - c)(b - d)(b - e)} \\
&\quad + \frac{c^5}{(c - a)(c - b)(c - d)(c - e)} + \frac{d^5}{(d - a)(d - b)(d - c)(d - e)} \\
&\quad + \frac{e^5}{(e - a)(e - b)(e - c)(e - d)}.
\end{align*}

solution:
First, we recognize that $\frac{4}{3x^{-3}}$ can be rewritten as $\frac{4x^3}{3}$. Thus, we have  \begin{align*}
\frac{4}{3x^{-3}} \cdot \frac{3x^{2}}{2} & = \frac{4x^3}{3} \cdot \frac{3x^2}{2} \\
& = \frac{(4 \cdot 3)(x^3 \cdot x^2)}{3 \cdot 2} \\
& = 2x^{3+2} \\
& = \boxed{2x^5}.
\end{align*}

